<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It suffices to show that the map $Y^{\natural } \rightarrow S$ has the right lifting property with respect to the inclusion 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  ( {X'}^{\natural } \times B^{\sharp } ) \coprod _{ {X'}^{\natural } \times A^{\sharp } } (X^{\natural } \times A^{\sharp }) \subseteq X^{\natural } \times B^{\sharp }, \]
</div>
    <p>
       for any anodyne inclusion of simplicial sets $A \subseteq B$. 
    <p>
      But this is a smash product of a marked cofibration ${X'}^{\natural } \rightarrow X^{\natural }$ (in $(\mSet )_{/S}$) and a trivial marked cofibration $A^{\sharp } \rightarrow B^{\sharp }$ ( in $\mSet $), and is therefore a trivial marked cofibration. We conclude by observing that $Y^{\natural }$ is a fibrant object of $(\mSet )_{/S}$ (Proposition <a href="/tag/D8B840" data-tag="D8B840">3.1.4.1</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
